  "name": "openmina",
  "description": "OpenMina is a modular implementation of the Mina protocol node in Rust, architected for high-performance block verification, transition frontier synchronization, and recursive SNARK generation. The project leverages a reactive action-reducer state machine to manage complex blockchain logic, including scan state transitions and staged ledger updates. It integrates a distributed P2P layer using libp2p and WebRTC, complemented by a comprehensive Angular-based real-time monitoring dashboard for network and resource visualization.",
